# The pistol, held on a target three units away that stands still: three
# shots take its shield (25 of 75 a shot, and the third's float error leaves a
# sliver for the body), then each of two takes half its health (a hit on the
# body costs half as much again as one on the shield), and the second kills.
# The trigger is let go before a shot that would hit the corpse, which the
# engine stops hitting after a second.
scenario pistol_kill
map bloodgulch
start flat_field 77.9 -166.2 0.32 0.0
target 81.0 -166.2 0.32 3.14159265
weapon weapons/pistol/pistol
ticks 160
# aim at the body
input 0 160 pitch=-0.13
input 60 100 fire=1

# the simulation holds to the engine's numbers to the last bit (a difference
# of 0 is what the first comparison found); the tolerances say so
tolerance position 0
tolerance velocity 0
tolerance facing 0
tolerance state 0
tolerance rounds 0
tolerance heat 0
tolerance shield 0
tolerance body 0
tolerance stun 0
tolerance life 0
tolerance hit 0
tolerance shots 0
tolerance age 0
